{
  "rationale": "The binding constraint is the system batch bound: a 1 MHz tick dumps 32 requests at once and the last result must land within 0.44 us, i.e. an effective burst rate of ~73 Msps. On Artix-7 only the 1-result/cycle families can reach that: pipelined (latency N+2, 1/cyc) and pipelined_m (latency ceil(N/m)+2, 1/cyc). iterative needs N+3 cyc/result and unrolled_k needs ceil(N/k)+3 cyc/result, so a 32-deep burst costs >=128-224 cycles and would require >290 MHz to clear 0.44 us - not reachable, so they only get small probe budgets to document infeasibility rather than a real share. Accuracy 2^-12 forces W>=14 (output LSB 2^-(W-2)) plus CORDIC residual, so N in the low-to-mid teens and a little angle/frac guard. The area objective (min LUTs+FFs) favours pipelined_m, which registers only every m stages and therefore carries far fewer FFs than the fully-registered pipelined chain, but its Fmax falls as m grows; pipelined has the best Fmax at the cost of N register banks. That Fmax-vs-FF trade between the two pipelined families (and m within pipelined_m) is where the Pareto front lives, so they take 85% of round 1. Round 1 deliberately spans W, N, guard and rounding so later rounds can tighten around the feasible region and then map the front over full ranges.",
